\ examples/deadline.telic, the translation of Infocom's Deadline, played from
\ deadline.stdin: the holes among the roses and the porcelain fragment in
\ them, Duffy's analysis of it, the lab report shown to Ms. Dunbar and her
\ accusation, her meeting with Baxter in the shed, the pistol shot upstairs,
\ the body in her room, and Baxter's arrest, which ends the case. The game
\ reads its arguments from args, redefined here to text frotz=1 width=80: in
\ the terminal, with the random numbers of the interpreter frotz started with
\ -s 1, so the transcript is release 28's apart from the banner and the
\ letter's indent.
: args ( -- arguments ) [ "text" "frotz=1" "width=80" ] ;

"../../examples/deadline.telic" load
